    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) as our premier offensive threat; he faces Quantrill with a massive 0.469 xwOBA, buoyed by a substantial SP skill edge that makes him our must-start anchor. Following closely is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12), whose profile is hyper-optimized for our needs: he benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Greene and, crucially, carries the elite sprint speed we prioritize for stolen base upside. While his 35% rain risk warrants monitoring, his scoring ceiling remains too high to bench, particularly given the aggressive dynamic platoon bump he receives today.\n\nOur middle-tier starters offer excellent value through situational matchups. **Trea Turner** (68.35) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.27) are high-floor pivots against Flaherty and Sears, respectively, with **Trea Turner** benefiting significantly from the leadoff spot and **Kazuma Okamoto** leveraging a favorable platoon advantage. **Chase Meidroth** (61.20) also presents an intriguing start; his score is driven by a 19% boost in SP skill against Lopez, providing surprising utility in a deep lineup. Conversely, we have opted to sit **Carson Benge** (47.06) on the bench. He was the closest consideration for the lineup, but concerns regarding Gray\u2019s 3.76 xERA and a concurrent 36% rain risk made him a secondary option compared to the higher efficiency ratings of **Luke Raley** and **Christian Yelich**.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for the Zebras. While **Christian Yelich** (53.55) projects as a marginal play due to a difficult matchup against Ashcraft\u2019s 3.22 xERA, we are leaning into the platoon advantage to keep him active. We are also keeping a close watch on **Kyle Schwarber** (60.06); despite an excellent xwOBA, his score is tempered by a poor BvP history against Flaherty. With **Lars Nootbaar** currently out of the lineup and our bench depth restricted, we are relying on this core to maintain our category leads while carefully balancing the game cap constraints essential for the long-term success of the Zurich Zebras.",
